    {
      "id": "87b65303-9bf9-4ff7-b98c-b77bce9209ca",
      "name": "OpenRouter \u2014 Score + Draft Reply",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "maxTries": 2,
      "position": [
        848,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are a senior small-business lead responder. Be helpful, natural, and concise.\n\nBusiness: {{ $json.businessName }}\nLead name: {{ $json.leadName }}\nEmail: {{ $json.leadEmail || \"not supplied\" }}\nPhone: {{ $json.leadPhone || \"not supplied\" }}\nMessage: {{ $json.leadMessage || \"No message supplied\" }}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with exactly these keys: {\"score\":\"hot|warm|cold\",\"need\":\"one concise sentence\",\"reply\":\"warm human reply under 80 words\"}. Mark hot only for clear urgency, immediate buying intent, or a high-value specific request. Do not promise prices, availability, or timings you cannot confirm.",
        "batching": {},
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "waitBetweenTries": 1000
    },
    {
      "id": "1a377af9-676b-44bd-ad8c-acec75f54dd8",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 624,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Speed-to-Lead Responder\n**Reply to every new lead in about 60 seconds.**\n\n### How it works\n1. A website form sends a new lead to the webhook.\n2. Your settings are applied and the lead data is cleaned.\n3. An AI model scores the lead (hot, warm or cold) and writes a short reply.\n4. The reply is emailed to the lead through Gmail.\n5. The lead is saved as a new row in Google Sheets.\n6. Hot leads trigger an instant alert to the owner.\n7. Any failure is logged and emailed to you.\n\n### Who it is for\nSmall businesses that lose leads by replying slowly, such as roofing, solar, HVAC, real estate and clinics.\n\n### Setup time\nAbout 10 minutes. See the Setup note below."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e7d3da5e-39b0-43a3-803d-fe295c46a133",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 624,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. Create a Google Sheet with two tabs named `Leads` and `Errors`.\n2. Type these headers in row 1, exactly as written (capital letters and spaces matter):\n   - **Leads:** Timestamp, Name, Email, Phone, Message, Score, Need, Reply Sent, Missing Fields\n   - **Errors:** Timestamp, Node, Error, Execution ID\n3. Connect your credentials: Gmail OAuth2, Google Sheets OAuth2 and an OpenRouter API key.\n4. In **Client Settings + Clean Lead**, replace the business name, owner email and sheet ID.\n5. Send a test lead to the Test URL, then publish and use the Production URL in your form.\n\n**Tip:** if your model cuts replies short, raise Max Tokens in the model node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "01d89eb7-5312-453e-a1c9-1a98b61722fc",
      "name": "Step 1 - Receive and clean the lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        272,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and clean the lead\nA webhook receives the form data (a POST request). The next node sets your business name, owner email and sheet ID, and cleans the lead fields.\n\n**You need to:** point your form to the Production URL and send `name`, `email`, `phone` and `message`. Edit the three settings in **Client Settings + Clean Lead**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "06d7ee61-e68f-4dba-86e8-d12cd1beae92",
      "name": "Step 2 - AI scores the lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        784,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## 2. AI scores the lead and writes the reply\nThe AI returns a score (hot, warm or cold), a one-line summary of the need, and a short friendly reply under 80 words. The code node checks the answer and uses a safe default reply if the AI output is broken.\n\n**You need to:** add your OpenRouter credential. Choose any chat model that can return JSON, and adjust the prompt to match your business."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "573b4d96-7e9d-4403-936b-de5e217da90c",
      "name": "Step 3 - Reply to the lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1376,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## 3. Reply to the lead\nIf the lead gave an email address, Gmail sends the AI-written reply right away. If not, the lead skips the email and goes straight to the sheet.\n\nIf the email fails, the lead is still saved and the owner is still alerted if the lead is hot. The error is logged.\n\n**You need to:** connect the Gmail account that should send replies."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0a955426-088c-433b-95aa-8e37c151d4e0",
      "name": "Step 4 - Save the lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1856,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 320,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## 4. Save the lead to Google Sheets\nEvery lead is added as a new row in the `Leads` tab: with a reply sent, with no email address, or with a failed email. The **Reply Sent** column says which.\n\n**You need to:** create the `Leads` tab with the exact headers from the Setup note."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "de3aa59d-5684-442e-8253-9308a21f4caa",
      "name": "Step 5 - Alert the owner",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2192,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 464,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## 5. Alert the owner about hot leads\nHot leads send an instant email to the owner with the contact details and the need. Warm and cold leads stop here.\n\n**You need to:** set the owner email in **Client Settings + Clean Lead**. You can swap Gmail for Slack or SMS."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "194d4acd-275a-49ee-8b88-bb6875ff557c",
      "name": "Step 6 - Error handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1056,
        912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 872,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## 6. Error handling\nIf any step fails, the error is prepared, saved in the `Errors` tab, and emailed to the owner with the failed node and execution ID.\n\n**You need to:** create the `Errors` tab with the headers Timestamp, Node, Error, Execution ID."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
